<title>USA: Copper stocks outside U.S. down in Oct. - ABMS.</title>
<headline>Copper stocks outside U.S. down in Oct. - ABMS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Refined copper stocks held by refineries outside the United States fell to 842,600 short tons at the end of October from a revised 826,800 short tons at the end of September, said the American Bureau of Metal Statistics.</p>
<p>London Metal Exchange stocks fell to 136,400 short tons in October from September's tally of 264,600 short tons.</p>
<p>Total refined copper stocks outside the U.S. fell to 979,000 short tons in October from a revised 1,090,800 short tons for the previous month.</p>
<p>--New York Commodity Desk 212-859-1640</p>
</text>
